      "content": "I hear you on the long-term aspect, but isn't there a danger in calling it 'temporary'? For many manufacturing sectors or middle-income families, a massive spike in energy costs isn't just a 'disruption'—it's a permanent loss of competitiveness or even a threat to their livelihood. Can we really justify prioritizing a future climate goal if it causes immediate, widespread economic hardship today?",
