    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds good in theory, but where is the money for all those subsidies and retraining programs supposed to come from if the economy is already struggling with high energy costs? it feels like the only real solution being offered is more government spending and debt, which just adds another layer of economic risk. isn't it more practical to pursue a gradual transition that adapts to market realities rather than forcing a massive, state-led overhaul?",
