      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument for a gradual, market-led transition is a classic case of \"sunk cost fallacy,\" where the short-term comfort of fossil fuel industries blinds us to the fact that their entire economic model is already collapsing under climate regulations. Governments must prioritize a swift, state-led overhaul because the market will never voluntarily reinvest in green infrastructure at the scale required to avert catastrophic climate damage; waiting for private capital to catch up guarantees that the transition will be too slow to save the planet. The money for subsidies and retraining must come from a massive tax on fossil fuel extraction and carbon-intensive industries, which are currently the primary beneficiaries of the status quo, rather than from general taxpayer debt.",
